{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793018594,"nonce":"rk2di5EHgj/j2Y2Va8pUToJQqjA=","title":"Studio: bound renderer allocations, idle work and resource lifetimes","message":"Status: planned; implementation has not started.\n\nParent: ashui:d2286369fcac837cdeee0b0dd26c05ba2aa86bbd4c967e330ef1471f26a61c68\nProgram epic: ashui:d2286369fcac837cdeee0b0dd26c05ba2aa86bbd4c967e330ef1471f26a61c68\nCross-repository integration: RayDE:c299bb980e54d48d600312f31a178213d13bc56bc2d3967c4bf42ef9816d6671\nPhase: 4\n\nScope\nHarden core preview rendering/inspection for repeated mount, rebuild, hide, show, resize and dispose. Track Owner/subscription/timer counts and GPU textures, glyph/image resources and transport caches. Implement dirty-driven updates, viewport culling and bounded retained snapshots; hidden/idle previews must not continually redraw. Document supported reuse and eviction policy per renderer/backend.\n\nAcceptance\nNative and browser stress fixtures return live object/resource counts to a defined steady state after repeated cycles. Active rendering, inspection and pan/zoom meet recorded frame budgets; idle previews sleep. Distinguish live retention from allocator high-water and include long-line/text/image-heavy nested-canvas cases.\n\nDepends on\n- ashui:be85b726001078af0db7f8ed83dae64d5b7ad267e941306e498e3ec3f1b6397e — Studio: expose typed component mounting and isolated preview contexts\n- ashui:3a53c8c3514ad635f0e9dd49d38bb3103ae58b25015363b0030e756241b511ea — Studio: implement a reusable subtree renderer for CanvasKit\n- ashui:cc768482633bd4848c842aff7f292f86fefe3828e55bc756b3488257673a044b — Studio: bridge canvas selection and Presentation input\n- ashui:bfb06d56f33c8185495b61e4f87629669136f53962479cf64576014fc6a6e6d2 — Studio: define cross-host render and inspection resource transport\n\nKeep implementation and validation evidence in this tracker. Follow the parent gate decisions; link any additional concrete runtime/backend prerequisite discovered by the feasibility work. No cloud deployment or new backend language is implied by this planning issue.","files":null}]}